-- Before downloading the django software. we have to create virtual environment.

-- venv ensures that the entire system is not containing the django software so that if there is any mismatch of the django version b/w 2 different projects then they will not get effected.

-- to create venv we have to follow the below steps 
1. create a project director.
2. Run "python -m venv venvName" -- creates venv in the director. 
3. Activate the venv by running the command "venvName\Scripts\activate" 
4. install django inside the venv.
"pip install django"
5. To see the installed django software run command -- "pip list"
6. If you run command -- "django-admin --version"

---------------------------------------

TO CREATE DJANGO PROJECT FOLLOW THE BELOW STEPS : 

1. Run command "django-admin startproject projectName"
2. To run the application we have to go to app directory then run command 
"python manage.py runserver"

NOTE : 
project -- application that we are working on.

app -- a module that belongs to the application.

manage.py -- helps to run our application

folder with the projectName -- main folder.

settings.py -- Here we configure the application. Encryp, Decrypt, database credentials

urls.py -- Here we map the requests and responses. 

-----------------------------------------

1. To create a new app we have to use command 

django-admin startapp appName

2. Register the app 
    -- go to settings -- installed apps -- add your app

3. create a view to handle request and response. 
    -- in our app we can find views.py
    -- inside it write the request handler method and send response.

4. create a url to view the created view. (app level url)
    -- create a file named urls.py

    urlpattern = [
        path('endpoint', view_name),
        .
        .
    ]

    -- after creating the app level urls we have to provide the app level url to module level url 

5. go to urls.py in our project folder. 
    -- we have to provide the app level urls to the project level url 
    -- we use include() to provide

    urlpattern = [
        ....,
        path('endpoint', include('appName.urls'))
    ]

6. after doing so just goto the location and then hit the endpoint and you will able to see the response.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

HTML pages as response. 

1. create a folder with a name templates in our app.
2. create html files inside the templates folder. 
3. use render function inside the view.py to send the html page. 
    syntax ; 
        def functionName(request):
            return render(request, 'htmlFilename.html")
4. register the view function with urls.py and hit the endpoint in the browser.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

REST FRAMEWORK : 

-- In python we use rest framework to generate the apis.
-- we have to install the rest framework 
    pip install djangorestframework
-- we have to register in installed apps.
-- we create a view to accept the request and to send a response.
    -- we used Response from rest_framework.response along with that we used rest_framework.decorators to use api_view.
    -- api_view defines when the view must be accessed inside it we pass the array of methods.
-- we have to register the view in urls.py 

